# Munir Visuals: Cursor rules
# Mirrors CLAUDE.md. If the two ever differ, CLAUDE.md is authoritative; report
# the difference rather than choosing silently.

## Read before any change
Read all six Context Architecture documents before implementing anything:
- docs/01_PRD.md      requirements and release gates
- docs/02_AppFlow.md  routes, screens, state machines
- docs/03_UI_Spec.md  design tokens and components
- docs/04_TRD.md      stack, endpoints, security, deployment, defects
- docs/05_Schema.md   tables and authorization model
- docs/06_Plan.md     task tracker and decision register
Also follow docs/DEVELOPMENT.md and the ADRs in docs/DECISIONS/.

## How to work
- Work only on an approved task ID from docs/06_Plan.md. If there is none, stop and ask.
- Ground every change in the repository: inspect the relevant source files first.
- Confirm the task's dependencies, check git status and the current branch, and
  review security and production risks.
- State a short plan, then make the smallest change that completes the task.
- Run the relevant tests: npm test, npm run typecheck, npm run lint,
  git diff --check, plus task-specific checks.
- After verified completion, update docs/06_Plan.md per its task-update
  procedure, and update docs 01-05 if a contract, route, schema, token, or flow changed.
- Report changed files, test counts, blockers, and git status. Never claim
  unverified success; write NOT RUN, BLOCKED, or UNVERIFIED.

## Never, without explicit owner authorization in the current task
- Access or write the production database, even read only.
- Create a production administrator.
- git push, merge branches, rewrite history, or force-push.
- Deploy, publish, or change Netlify configuration or its Auto Publishing lock.
- Record a legal approval in src/content/legal.tsx, or open inquiry intake.
- Read .env.local, .env, or any .env.* other than .env.example.
- Expose secret values anywhere.
- Make architecture changes outside the task scope (propose an ADR instead).
- Commit, unless the task authorizes it.
- Send real email or real Turnstile requests.
- Run integration:identity or integration:run (database work is postponed).

## Facts that are easy to get wrong
- Published = main@288fde6 (owner-reported); main = 1797766 (unpublished);
  10f09b4..4f7f564 are local only. Never call a local fix deployed.
- Authorization is server-side only; middleware checks cookie presence only;
  no PostgreSQL row-level security exists.
- Build-time environment checks must use the literal process.env.NODE_ENV.
- Inquiry intake opens only through legal approvals; there is no switch.
- Never add loading.tsx to the public route group (soft-404 risk).
- A full next build needs a reachable database; never use production for it.
- Dark-only design, square corners, no shadows; use the tokens in src/app/globals.css.
